# Independent Qwen3.5-4B test lane; baseline cloud lock remains unchanged.
#
# vLLM is a runtime dependency of this lane only. The Qwen2.5-VL-7B lane keeps
# torch 2.7.1 + Transformers 4.57.6 and must never receive this package.
#
# vLLM is pinned to 0.19.1 because it is the last release whose shipped binary
# links libcudart.so.12. Reading the Python metadata is NOT sufficient to tell
# a usable vLLM from a broken one; the CUDA major version lives in the compiled
# extension. DT_NEEDED of vllm/_C.abi3.so, extracted from the published wheels:
#
#     vllm 0.19.1  ->  libcudart.so.12   (works on this CUDA 12.8 host)
#     vllm 0.20.2  ->  libcudart.so.13
#     vllm 0.21.0  ->  libcudart.so.13
#
# 0.20.0 is the real cutover, not 0.22.1. A wheel linking libcudart.so.13 fails
# immediately on a CUDA 12 host with:
#     ImportError: libcudart.so.13: cannot open shared object file
# Kaggle's T4 is SM 7.5 on a CUDA 12.8 driver, so only the CUDA 12 line works.
#
# vLLM 0.19.1 pins torch==2.10.0 / torchvision==0.25.0 and requires
# transformers>=4.56, satisfied by 5.17.0. The torch pin is built for cu128 to
# match the host toolkit (torch.version.cuda == 12.8).
Pillow==12.3.0
PyYAML==6.0.3
setuptools==78.1.0
torch==2.10.0+cu128
torchvision==0.25.0+cu128
transformers==5.17.0
accelerate==1.12.0
vllm==0.19.1
